    "slug": "oic-condemns-houthi-attacks-on-mecca-and-medina",
    "summary": "The Organisation of Islamic Cooperation strongly condemned Houthi attacks on Mecca and Medina, calling them violations of holy sites and a threat to civilian safety.",
    "content": "The General Secretariat of the Organisation of Islamic Cooperation (OIC) has issued a strong condemnation of attacks it attributes to the Houthi group on the holy city of Mecca and the Medina region in Saudi Arabia. In a statement released on Tuesday, the OIC described the attacks as a serious violation of the sanctity of the holy sites and a source of fear for civilians.\n\nThe OIC, which represents 57 Muslim-majority countries, said the attacks also targeted ongoing operations in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia. It emphasized that such acts undermine the sanctity of mosques and holy places, and offend the sentiments of Muslims worldwide. The organization called for an immediate halt to these actions.\n\nThe Houthi group, which controls parts of Yemen, has been involved in a prolonged conflict with a Saudi-led coalition since 2015. While the Houthis have previously launched cross-border attacks into Saudi Arabia, this is the first time the OIC has explicitly condemned attacks on Mecca and Medina, the two holiest cities in Islam.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this development is particularly significant. Somalia is a member of the OIC, and many Somalis hold deep religious and cultural ties to the holy cities. Any threat to these sites resonates strongly within the community, which often looks to the OIC for leadership on issues affecting the Muslim world. The condemnation also highlights the broader regional instability that can impact diaspora communities through family ties and remittances.\n\nThe OIC's statement did not specify the exact timing or nature of the attacks, but it underscored the need for unity among Muslim nations in protecting holy sites. The organization reiterated its support for Saudi Arabia's efforts to ensure the safety of pilgrims and residents.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/09/16/ururka-iskaashiga-islaamka-oo-cambaareeyay-weerarrada-xuutiyiinta-ee-maka-iyo-madiina/",
